- Recompiling ADS applications for IntelliCAD

	- Use Visual C++ 4.0, 4.1, 4.2, or 5.0.

	- Create a new project.  After specifying a project name, select 
	  Project type:  Dynamic-Link Library.

	- After creating the project, select your project files.  Along with
	  the C files and LIBs used for your ADS application.

	- Add the file "sds.lib" to your project.  This file can be found in the 
        ICAD\API\SDS directory.  This will link in the necessary file needed to 
        create the DLL.

	- Add the file "entpoint.c" to your project.  This file can be found in the 
        ICAD\API\SDS directory.  This will provide an entry point for your DLL. NOTE:
        This file may NOT be necessary in later version of IntelliCAD, so if you have 
        problems remove this file from your project.

	- Modify your C or CPP files to include sds.h instead of adslib.h.  This file 
        can be found in the ICAD\API\SDS directory.  

	- In the Project Settings dialog, the following modifications need to 
	  be made to the default settings:

		- Debug:

			- Add \ICAD\ICAD.EXE to the "Executable for Debug Session" edit
			  box.

		- C/C++ Settings:

			- Catagory: 
				
				Preprocessor - Add "SDS_MEMORY" to Preprocessor Definitions.
				             - Add the \ICAD\API\SDS directory to Additional 
							   Include Directories.

		- Link Settings:

			- Catagory:

				Customize - Check the box "Force file output".

	    
